e  not going to use and you have to you  know take back or sell so i don't i  don't like spending money till I find a  way to make money off of it so I started  off just me with my flip camera you know  you know wobbly camera and terrible  lighting and slowly I invested more and  back into it now I use just a sony  camcorder  from costco that i picked up it's on a  tripod that I picked up at a camera  store and I use a microphone that  connects so you can see here I've got a  little bit of a microphone coming up  through my sweater here and it did that  because people were complaining that the  feedback the quality of the sound wasn't  fantastic coming from a flip camera and  so I just found the the highest-end  costco camera that had external  microphone jack like to plug into in  terms of the workflow I just save  questions that come to me from my  readers and i would put them on my phone  and then i save them for the week and  then I just kind of go through them and  once a week I I sit here at my house on  a Wednesday and fire up fire up the  camera get a cappuccino ready to go so I  have a little bit more energy and drink  it back and start answering questions  and so if you're just getting started  you may not have an audience yet to pull  from right now with the questions that  come in to me are from my readers or  Facebook fans or YouTube video Watchers  all over the place which is awesome but  if you don't have that audience yet you  can build it up and basically go out and  look for questions you could join  different forms or different Facebook  groups or LinkedIn groups and see what  kinds of questions people are asking and  say that you're going to make a video  response for them and so hopefully then  they'll you know watch it when you  actually do create it may be spread the  word a little bit about it but that  would be how i would get started if i  didn't already have an audience to be  able to pull questions from so hopefully  that helps good luck 